---
title: Permissions
# Who may do what in the personal area: per Discord role and per person
# (server/permissions.js, /api/app/permissions). Shown to those holding
# `manage`; the shared admin account always may.
tool: settings
tab: permissions
pageTitle: Permissions
wide: true
permalink: /app/settings/permissions/
noindex: true
excludeFromSitemap: true
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
seoTitle: 'Permissions | AI Safety for Italy'
---
{% extends "app.njk" %}
{% block page %}
    <div class="perm-page" id="permPage">
      <p class="form-note" id="permLocked" hidden>You can change the Site content and Settings columns. The other columns open personal data (mentorship, form answers, member applications): only the shared admin can change them.</p>

      <section class="panel">
        <div class="panel-head">
          <h2>Discord roles</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="panel-note" style="margin-top:0">Everyone with a role gets what it allows. A member with several roles gets what all of them allow together. Roles are read from Discord at each sign-in and again every few minutes.</p>
        <div class="results-wrap" id="roleTable"></div>
        <p class="form-note" id="noBot" hidden>The Discord bot is not set up here, so the server’s roles cannot be listed. Add a role by its id (Discord → Server settings → Roles → ⋯ → Copy role ID).</p>
        <form class="form-row" id="addRole" style="margin-top:1rem" hidden>
          <div>
            <label class="form-label" for="roleId">Role id</label>
            <input class="form-input is-compact" id="roleId" required pattern="[0-9]{5,25}">
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="form-label" for="roleName">Role name</label>
            <input class="form-input is-compact" id="roleName" required maxlength="100">
          </div>
          <div style="align-self:end"><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" type="submit">Add role</button></div>
        </form>
      </section>

      <section class="panel">
        <div class="panel-head">
          <h2>People</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="panel-note" style="margin-top:0">For one person, on top of what their roles allow: what you tick here adds to their roles, it never takes anything away. Only people who have signed in here once can be added.</p>
        <div class="results-wrap" id="peopleTable"></div>
        <form class="form-row" id="addPerson" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <div>
            <label class="form-label" for="personPick">Person</label>
            <select class="form-input is-compact" id="personPick" required></select>
          </div>
          <div style="align-self:end"><button class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" type="submit">Add person</button></div>
        </form>
      </section>

      <div class="form-error" id="permError" role="alert" hidden></div>
      <div class="action-bar">
        <p>Changes apply within a few minutes, and at once from the next sign-in.</p>
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="savePerms">Save permissions</button>
      </div>
    </div>

<script src="/assets/js/meet/common.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/meet/app-common.js" defer></script>
<script src="/assets/js/meet/settings-permissions.js" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
